  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist.\n\n**Data exploration.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) has a `timestamp` time field. The main fields are:\n- `response` (string, with `response.keyword`) holds the HTTP status code.\n- `bytes` is the response size.\n- `clientip` is the client IP.\n- `geo.dest` is the destination country.\n- `url`, `host`, `agent`, and `extension` describe the request.\n\nI could not check the actual `response` value distribution. The Kibana console proxy and the ES|QL endpoint are disabled on this instance, so I relied on the field metadata.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-1b53333e Web logs overview\"** (`eff-1b53333e-web-logs-overview-a025f940912a`, last 7 days)\n1. Total requests (count)\n2. Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n3. Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n4. Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n5. Requests by response code (bar, terms on `response.keyword`)\n6. Top countries by requests (table, terms on `geo.dest`)\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-1b53333e 5xx spike\"** (id `0589db96-f55d-40f4-b573-8c0f0a006b12`)\n- Type `.es-query` (DSL), consumer `stackAlerts`, tag `EFF-1b53333e`.\n- Query: `response.keyword` wildcard `5*`, on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10 over a 5-minute window, checked every 1 minute.\n- It is enabled, and its status is currently `ok`.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- The rule has no action connector, so it records alerts but sends no notifications. I did not create one, since none was requested.\n- I enabled the rule so it actually runs every minute. The tool's default is disabled.\n- `response` is a string, so the 5xx match uses a wildcard on the keyword field rather than a numeric range.",
